{"name":"Outer Rim","hex":"#221177","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"outer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Outside; external.","Farther from the centre of the inside."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer part.","An uncovered section of the seating at a stadium or sportsground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outer"},{"term":"rim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Nyaturu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edge around something, especially when circular.","A wheelrim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of Star Wars planets and moons","blocks":[{"text":"The Universe of the Star Wars franchise features multiple planets and moons. While only the feature films and some other works are considered canon to the franchise since the 2012 acquisition of Lucasfilm by The Walt Disney Company, some canon planets were first named or explored in works from the non-canon Star Wars expanded universe, now rebranded as Star Wars Legends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Galaxymap_p1.svg/330px-Galaxymap_p1.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Star_Wars_planets_and_moons","wikidata":"Q2294199"},{"title":"Rim (wheel)","blocks":[{"text":"The rim is the \"outer edge of a wheel, holding the tire\". It makes up the outer circular design of the wheel on which the inside edge of the tire is mounted on vehicles such as automobiles. For example, on a bicycle wheel the rim is a large hoop attached to the outer ends of the spokes of the wheel that holds the tire and tube. In cross-section, the rim is deep in the center and shallow at the outer edges, thus forming a \"U\" shape that supports the bead of the tire casing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/ATV_Rim_Lip_Parts.jpg/330px-ATV_Rim_Lip_Parts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rim_(wheel)","wikidata":"Q54278667"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/ESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg/500px-ESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/ESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg/1280px-ESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/ESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg/500px-ESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ESO artist's impression of OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb, an exoplanet compared to the ice planet Hoth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AESO_OGLE-2005-BLG-390Lb.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Felge-querschnitt.jpg/500px-Felge-querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Felge-querschnitt.jpg/1280px-Felge-querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Felge-querschnitt.jpg/500px-Felge-querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross section of a bicycle rim","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFelge-querschnitt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/16-11-18-Holzfelge_mit_Schlauchreifen-RR2_7364.jpg/500px-16-11-18-Holzfelge_mit_Schlauchreifen-RR2_7364.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/16-11-18-Holzfelge_mit_Schlauchreifen-RR2_7364.jpg/1280px-16-11-18-Holzfelge_mit_Sch